---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Legal & data handling · borck.consulting" description="How borck.consulting handles client information. The data-handling commitment is part of the value.">

  <div class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Legal &amp; data handling</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">How this practice handles your information.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      The data-handling commitment applies the practice's thesis to its own operations.
      It is part of why a regulated firm would work with this practice rather than another.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="data-handling-block">
    <h2>The commitment</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--gray-1); line-height: 1.65;">
      When working with this practice, your firm's documents, names, and matter
      details may pass through review. The following commitments apply to all
      engagements:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Local-only AI processing.</strong> Any AI assistance used on client
        material runs on local models on encrypted hardware. Client material is
        not uploaded to ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or any other cloud LLM.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Encrypted storage.</strong> All client material is held on encrypted
        disks. There is no cloud sync of client folders.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>90-day retention.</strong> Client material is retained for 90 days
        after engagement close, then deleted, unless you request otherwise in writing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No case studies without consent.</strong> The practice does not
        publish your firm's name, sector, or any identifying detail without written
        consent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>NDA available on request.</strong> A standard mutual NDA is available
        and can be signed before substantive discussion.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
    <p>
      This page sets out how `borck.consulting` collects, uses, and stores personal
      information, in line with the Australian Privacy Principles under the Privacy
      Act 1988 (Cth).
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--gray-2);">
      Last updated 31 October 2026.
    </p>
    <h3>What is collected</h3>
    <p>
      Information you provide through the contact form on this site (name, firm, email
      address, and the message you send), information you provide by email, and any
      material shared in the course of an engagement. The contact form is served from
      <code>forms.borck.consulting</code>. The practice does not use a third-party
      booking service.
    </p>
    <h3>How it is used</h3>
    <p>
      Information is used to respond to your inquiry, to deliver engaged services,
      and to maintain the records required for tax, GST, and professional indemnity
      compliance. Information is not sold or rented. It is shared with the service
      providers listed below only to deliver and protect the contact channel.
    </p>
    <h3>Storage and retention</h3>
    <p>
      Contact form submissions are stored on the practice's server for 90 days, then
      deleted. Email correspondence is retained while it remains relevant, and
      otherwise deleted within twelve months. Engagement material is retained for
      90 days after engagement close, then deleted, except where you have requested
      otherwise or where retention is required for compliance (for example, tax
      records under the relevant statutory periods).
    </p>
    <h3>Service providers</h3>
    <p>
      Resend delivers contact form messages to the practice. Purelymail hosts the
      practice mailbox at <code>michael@borck.dev</code>. Cloudflare provides DNS and
      security filtering for <code>forms.borck.consulting</code>. These providers
      process information only to deliver and protect the contact channel.
    </p>
    <h3>Access and correction</h3>
    <p>
      You may request access to information held about you, or correction of any
      information that is inaccurate. Requests should be sent to
      <a href="mailto:michael@borck.dev">michael@borck.dev</a>.
    </p>
    <h3>Complaints</h3>
    <p>
      If you have a complaint about how your information has been handled, please
      contact the practice in the first instance. Complaints can also be made to
      the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).
    </p>

    <h2>Terms of engagement (summary)</h2>
    <p>
      The terms below summarise the practice's standard engagement structure. The
      binding terms for any specific engagement are set out in the Master Services
      Agreement and Statement of Work signed between the parties.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Engagements are fixed-scope and fixed-price.</li>
      <li>Payment is 50% deposit on signing and 50% on delivery, unless otherwise specified in the SOW. Net-7 invoice terms.</li>
      <li>Intellectual property: client work product is owned by the client. The practice retains its own framework and methodology IP.</li>
      <li>Limitation of liability: the practice's liability is limited to the amount paid under the engagement, and is in any event limited to the cover of the practice's professional indemnity insurance.</li>
      <li>Governing law: Western Australia, Australia.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      The principal of this practice, Michael Borck, is also a Lecturer at Curtin
      University, where he teaches AI and cyber security. The practice operates privately, on
      personal time and infrastructure, and is <strong>not affiliated with or
      endorsed by Curtin University</strong>. The relationship is disclosed to
      Curtin in accordance with the University's Disclosure of Relationships and
      Interests procedures.
    </p>

    <h2>Business details</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>ABN:</strong> 73 749 768 332<br />
